    </release>
    <release version="0.15.1" date="2026-10-16">
      <description>
        <p>Fixes</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Fixed the macOS app quitting unexpectedly</li>
          <li>Fixed the app crashing repeatedly a few seconds after</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="0.15.0" date="2026-10-16">
      <description>
        <p>New</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Right-click a contact (or Command-click on a Mac) to email,</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Fixes</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Folder unread counts now match across devices, and emails read on another device show as read</li>
          <li>Fixed unread counts that differed between devices,</li>
          <li>Fixed new encrypted messages showing a loading</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="0.14.32" date="2026-10-14">
      <description>
        <p>Fixes</p>
        <ul>
          <li>If the app keeps going blank right after it opens, it now shows a troubleshooting page with diagnostics and a reset, instead of reloading forever</li>
          <li>New Help &gt; Troubleshooting menu item</li>
          <li>Turning off App Lock no longer hangs on a large mailbox. Cached mail</li>
          <li>New mail for another signed-in account now shows a notice that names the</li>
          <li>Accounts added with an API key no longer get stuck when opening a</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="0.14.31" date="2026-10-12">
      <description>
        <p>Fixes</p>
        <ul>
          <li>The app no longer shows a blank screen while it starts</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="0.14.30" date="2026-10-12">
      <description>
        <p>Fixes</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Conversations stay together and match Thunderbird and other mail apps. Most noticeable on mobile, where replies could split into separate threads</li>
          <li>Replies to an email you sent now join the same conversation as your Sent copy</li>
          <li>Replying from an account that isn't on screen still marks the original email as replied</li>
          <li>A send retried after a dropped connection no longer shows as failed when the email already went out</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
